    "section": "1.82",
    "heading": "Mounting and Dismounting",
    "lineStart": 1550,
    "lineEnd": 1552
  },
  "section": "1.82",
  "rulesText": "During your move, you can mount a creature that is within 5 feet of you or dismount. Doing so costs an amount of movement equal to half your Speed (round down). For example, if your Speed is 30 feet, you spend 15 feet of movement to mount a horse."
}
